This product bundles third-party material beyond its Python and JavaScript
dependencies. Each item below travels inside the built web bundle or the
published wheel, so its notice travels here.

**Font Awesome Free 5.15.4** (https://fontawesome.com), reached through
`@jupyter-widgets/html-manager`, which the notebook widget renderer uses for its
icons. The webfonts under `web/dist/assets/fa-*` are covered by three licences
at once, as Font Awesome distributes them: the icons under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), the fonts under SIL OFL 1.1
(https://scripts.sil.org/OFL), and the accompanying code under the MIT licence.
CC BY 4.0 asks for attribution, which is what this paragraph is.

**Geist** (https://vercel.com/font), Copyright (c) 2023 Vercel, Inc., SIL OFL 1.1
(https://scripts.sil.org/OFL). The interface is set in Geist and Geist Mono, loaded
from Google Fonts, and the "elbi" wordmark under `web/public/brand` and in
`web/src/components/Logo.tsx` is its outlines converted to paths.

**KaTeX** (https://katex.org), Copyright (c) 2013-2020 Khan Academy and other
contributors, MIT licensed. Its math webfonts ship under
`web/dist/assets/KaTeX_*` and render mathematics in notebook and chat output.

**PostHog** (https://posthog.com), Copyright (c) 2020-2026 PostHog Inc., MIT
licensed. The warehouse "Sources" surface follows PostHog's Lemon UI for its
layout, density and control shapes, and
`packages/elbi/web/src/components/warehouse/phc.tsx` derives spacing and sizing
values, and its success/danger/info colours, from that stylesheet. The accent
and brand colours are this product's own.

**Apache Ossie**, formerly the Open Semantic Interchange
(https://github.com/open-semantic-interchange/OSI), Apache-2.0 licensed. The
metrics layer vendors its JSON Schema at
`packages/elbi-core/src/elbi_core/spec/osi.schema.json` so an installed wheel can
validate an OSI document without reaching the network.

