Some dependencies installed alongside this product are copyleft, and a
distribution that bundles them (the container image, chiefly) carries their
terms rather than this product's.

Under the LGPL: fpdf2 (certificate PDFs), psycopg and psycopg-binary (the
Postgres driver), psycopg2-binary (reached through MLflow's registry), pymssql
(the SQL Server connector), paramiko (the SFTP connector, reached through
fsspec) and yattag. Each is imported as a separate library
and none is modified here, so the LGPL's terms attach to those libraries alone.
They install as ordinary packages in the environment, which is what lets a
recipient replace one with their own build, as the LGPL requires.

Under the MPL 2.0, in whole or in part: certifi, pathspec, orjson and tqdm. The
MPL applies per file and none of those files is modified here.

Nothing in this product is licensed under the GPL, the AGPL, the SSPL or a
non-commercial licence. Where a dependency offers a choice (dompurify as
MPL-2.0 or Apache-2.0, jszip as MIT or GPL-3.0-or-later) this product elects
the permissive option.

